<LegalLayout
  title="SMS Opt-In & Messaging Program"
  description="How Sooppiy collects consent to send SMS, with screenshots of the in-app opt-in flow."
  lastUpdated="July 21, 2026"
>

<div class="legal-notice">
  <p>
    This page documents how end users give consent to receive text messages
    from Sooppiy. The opt-in itself happens inside the Sooppiy web app after
    sign-in; because that screen requires authentication, the full flow is
    reproduced here with screenshots for carrier and campaign review.
  </p>
</div>

<h2>1. What We Send</h2>
<p>
  Sooppiy sends two kinds of transactional text messages, and nothing else:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>One-time verification codes (OTP)</strong> used to verify the phone number and sign-in activity.</li>
  <li><strong>Account alerts</strong> the user has switched on in their notification settings (trade and risk alerts for their own account).</li>
</ul>
<p>
  We do not send marketing or promotional SMS, and we do not share phone
  numbers with third parties for their marketing purposes. Message frequency
  varies with the user's own activity and alert settings. Message and data
  rates may apply.
</p>

<h2>2. How Users Opt In</h2>
<ol>
  <li>
    The user creates an account at
    <a href="https://sooppiy.com/sign-up">https://sooppiy.com/sign-up</a>
    (email + verification code, or Google sign-in). No phone number is
    collected at sign-up.
  </li>
  <li>
    After signing in, the user opens <strong>Account Settings</strong> at
    <a href="https://sooppiy.com/settings">https://sooppiy.com/settings</a>
    and finds the <strong>"Phone number for SMS"</strong> card.
  </li>
  <li>
    The user enters their mobile number and actively checks a consent
    checkbox that is <strong>unchecked by default</strong>. The phone number
    cannot be saved while the checkbox is unchecked.
  </li>
  <li>
    Only after this explicit consent is stored does Sooppiy send any SMS to
    that number. Consent (and its timestamp) is recorded with the user's
    account.
  </li>
</ol>

<h2>3. Consent Language Shown in the App</h2>
<blockquote>
  <p>
    "I agree to receive SMS verification codes and account alerts from
    Sooppiy at this number. Message frequency varies. Message &amp; data
    rates may apply. Reply STOP to unsubscribe, HELP for help."
  </p>
</blockquote>
<p>
  The checkbox links directly to our
  <a href="https://sooppiy.com/privacypolicy">Privacy Policy</a> and
  <a href="https://sooppiy.com/termsconditions">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.
</p>

